Z||000000||Captain Midnight||09-06-2001||01:07 AM||||I see that the '88 5-speed Getrag was ofered in two ratios. I would like to change mine to the lower final drive ratio. Are those tranys rare to find used? Where could I find just the ring and gear.<BR>Thanks <P>------------------<BR>Captain Midnight||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-06-2001||01:22 AM||||I'm not sure about the 88 Getrag having two different ratios. Olds did make an Achieva SCX with a 3.91 geared Getrag with limited slip differential! You can spot an SCX by the 14 in. aluminum wheels and dual rectangular exhaust cutouts in the rear bumper. Nice trans for a Fiero.<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||09-06-2001||03:04 PM||||Actually the SCX is a quad 4 tranny, which will not bolt up to the 2.8.<P>SFAIK, Fiero Getrag's only had one ratio, 3.61:1 or was it 3.64:1?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||lou_dias||09-06-2001||03:22 PM||||It was actually 3.65<BR>3.61 is the 4 speed v6 isuzu trans ratio<P>Look up the 88 Beretta and Cavalier 5 speeds with the v6 if you see 2, one will be a 3.42 and the other a 3.65  then you flip one of the arms 180 degeers and your done.  I think Rodney Dickman offers a kit for certain years 89+ I think.||||reg||1
